Learn how it works.

00:25:03.800 --> 00:25:08.640
To understand how your code works you need to step back and think about what a programming

00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:11.160
language is.

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:15.800
Consider how your code communicates commands to the computer.

00:25:15.800 --> 00:25:18.400
What is a programming language?

00:25:18.400 --> 00:25:22.640
Programming languages like C sharp let you write instructions that you want the computer

00:25:22.640 --> 00:25:24.320
to carry out.

00:25:24.320 --> 00:25:28.800
Each programming language has its own syntax but after learning your first programming

00:25:28.800 --> 00:25:33.640
language and attempting to learn another one you'll quickly realize that they all share

00:25:33.640 --> 00:25:35.560
many similar concepts.

00:25:35.560 --> 00:25:40.440
A programming language's job is to allow a human to express their intent in a human

00:25:40.440 --> 00:25:42.880
readable and understandable way.

00:25:42.880 --> 00:25:49.120
The instructions you write in a programming language are called source code or just code.

00:25:49.120 --> 00:25:50.880
Software developers write code.

00:25:50.880 --> 00:25:55.800
At this point a developer can update and change the code but the computer can't understand

00:25:55.800 --> 00:25:56.800
the code.

00:25:56.800 --> 00:26:04.320
The code first must be compiled into a format that the computer can understand.

00:26:04.320 --> 00:26:06.600
What is compilation?

00:26:06.600 --> 00:26:12.080
A special program called a compiler converts your source code into a different format that

00:26:12.080 --> 00:26:16.480
the computer's central processing unit CPU can execute.

00:26:16.480 --> 00:26:22.160
When you used the green run button in the previous unit the code you wrote was first

00:26:22.160 --> 00:26:25.120
compiled then executed.

00:26:25.120 --> 00:26:28.080
Why does code need to be compiled?

00:26:28.080 --> 00:26:33.560
Although most programming languages seem cryptic at first they can be more easily understood

00:26:33.560 --> 00:26:37.880
by humans than the computer's preferred language.

00:26:37.880 --> 00:26:43.920
The CPU understands instructions that are expressed by turning thousands or millions

00:26:43.920 --> 00:26:49.880
of tiny switches either on or off.

00:26:49.880 --> 00:26:54.920
Compilers bridge these two worlds by translating your human readable instructions into a

00:26:54.920 --> 00:26:59.040
computer understandable set of instructions.

00:26:59.040 --> 00:27:00.760
What is syntax?

00:27:00.760 --> 00:27:04.200
The rules for writing C-sharp code is called syntax.

00:27:04.200 --> 00:27:09.280
Just like human languages have rules regarding punctuation and sentence structure computer

00:27:09.280 --> 00:27:12.200
programming languages also have rules.

00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:18.080
Those rules define the keywords and operators of C-sharp and how they are put together to

00:27:18.080 --> 00:27:20.520
form programs.

00:27:20.520 --> 00:27:26.560
When you wrote code into the.NET editor you may have noticed subtle changes to the color

00:27:26.560 --> 00:27:29.240
of different words and symbols.

00:27:29.240 --> 00:27:34.440
Syntax highlighting is a helpful feature that you'll begin to use to easily spot mistakes

00:27:34.440 --> 00:27:41.920
in your code that don't conform to the syntax rules of C-sharp.

