When the phrase is surrounded by double quotation marks in your C-sharp code it's called a

00:28:00.760 --> 00:28:02.720
literal string.

00:28:02.720 --> 00:28:12.880
In other words you literally wanted the characters H-E-L-L-O and so on sent to the output.

00:28:12.880 --> 00:28:15.680
The console part is called a class.

00:28:15.680 --> 00:28:22.560
Classes own methods or you could say the methods live inside a class.

00:28:22.560 --> 00:28:26.360
To visit the method you must know which class it's in.

00:28:26.360 --> 00:28:30.080
For now think of a class as a way to represent an object.

00:28:30.080 --> 00:28:35.920
In this case all of the methods that operate on your output console are defined inside

00:28:35.920 --> 00:28:37.760
the console class.

00:28:37.760 --> 00:28:43.560
There's also a dot or period that separates the class name console and the method name

00:28:43.560 --> 00:28:44.920
write line.

00:28:44.920 --> 00:28:47.480
The period is the member access operator.

00:28:47.480 --> 00:28:52.280
In other words the dot is how you navigate from the class to one of its methods.

00:28:52.280 --> 00:28:55.960
The write line part is called a method.

00:28:55.960 --> 00:29:00.880
You can always spot a method because it has a set of parentheses after it.

00:29:00.880 --> 00:29:02.880
Each method has one job.

00:29:02.880 --> 00:29:09.440
The write line methods job is to write a line of data to the output console.

00:29:09.440 --> 00:29:15.280
The data that's printed is sent in between the opening and closing parentheses of an

00:29:15.280 --> 00:29:18.480
input parameter.

00:29:18.480 --> 00:29:22.480
Some methods need input parameters while others don't.

00:29:22.480 --> 00:29:27.440
But if you want to invoke a method you must always use the parentheses after the methods

00:29:27.440 --> 00:29:35.520
name the parentheses are known as the method invocation operator.

00:29:35.520 --> 00:29:39.480
Finally the semicolon is the end of statement operator.

00:29:39.480 --> 00:29:43.080
A statement is a complete instruction in C sharp.

00:29:43.080 --> 00:29:49.400
The semicolon tells the compiler that you finished entering the command.

